ProsperoSunshine: the GameStream HTTPS and RTSP servers stop without racing their accept

Both are stopped from another thread than the one that runs them, and both accept again from the handler of the last
accept, on the acceptor that the stop closes: asio allows neither on one object from two threads at once. The HTTP server
on 47989 crashed the host that way while it stopped (Simple-Web-Server patch 0005, which gives ServerBase the
acceptor_mutex). SunshineHTTPSServer has an accept() of its own for the client certificate check; it takes the same lock
and leaves a closed acceptor alone. The RTSP server is no Simple-Web-Server one: rtsp::start now only stops the
io_context from its thread (io_context::stop is safe from any thread), waits for the handler thread to leave its loop,
and calls stop(), which closes the acceptor, after that. bind() restarts the context for a start after rest mode, as
before.

--- a/src/nvhttp.cpp
+++ b/src/nvhttp.cpp
@@ -139,6 +139,12 @@
      * @details Keep each handler's scope guard alive until all access to the server has finished.
      */
     void accept() override {
+      // ProsperoSunshine: start() runs this on the server's thread, called again from the last accept's handler, while
+      // stop() comes from nvhttp::start's thread; the two take turns on the acceptor (Simple-Web-Server patch 0005).
+      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> acceptor_lock(acceptor_mutex);
+      if (!acceptor->is_open()) {
+        return;
+      }
       auto connection = create_connection(*io_service, context);
 
       acceptor->async_accept(connection->socket->lowest_layer(), [this, connection](const SimpleWeb::error_code &ec) {
--- a/src/rtsp.cpp
+++ b/src/rtsp.cpp
@@ -735,6 +735,13 @@
     }
 
     /**
+     * @brief Make iterate() return at once; safe from any thread, unlike stop().
+     */
+    void interrupt() {
+      io_context.stop();
+    }
+
+    /**
      * @brief Stop the RTSP server.
      */
     void stop() {
@@ -1418,8 +1425,12 @@
     shutdown_event->view();
 
     // Stop the server and join the server thread
-    server.stop();
+    // ProsperoSunshine: the acceptor belongs to the handler thread, whose handle_accept() calls async_accept on it, and
+    // asio allows no close() from here meanwhile. So the context is only stopped from here (the loop sees the shutdown
+    // event and ends), and the acceptor is closed once that thread has ended.
+    server.interrupt();
     rtsp_thread.join();
+    server.stop();
   }
 
